# DIAGNOSTICS

`CROI_ERR_BAD_HANDLE`, `CROI_ERR_WRONG_TYPE` and `CROI_ERR_ACCESS_DENIED` as for any handle; see syscall(2).
A resource of the wrong kind given to a call is `CROI_ERR_WRONG_TYPE`, and one that does not cover the range is `CROI_ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE`.
`CROI_ERR_NO_MEMORY`: no memory.

